The gateway 10.1.0.1 is a VRRP VIP managed by keepalived, correctly configured and stable. The claim of periodic outage has no confirmed mechanism (no flap script, no VRRP state changes, no carrier events). The confirmed real anomaly is the ACL — it silently drops all TCP/UDP from Office A to Office B while ICMP passes, causing application connections to hang/timeout. This matches the infra_sweep flag and is confirmed on both distribution switches.

This anomaly belongs to the **acl-skill** family (selective protocol drop via iptables).

